---
import OffClockPage from '../../components/OffClockPage.astro';
import { smallFavoritesSection } from '../../data/off-the-clock';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<OffClockPage heading={smallFavoritesSection.title} description={smallFavoritesSection.description} noIndex>
  <details class="favorite" name="small-favorites">
    <summary>Ganeshas of Mumbai</summary>
    <div class="bio">
      <p>
        My cousin in Mumbai got me curious about the history behind the city's Ganesh idols.
        He'd already found out quite a bit about some of them, and I wanted to see what else I could find.
        That's how Ganeshas of Mumbai started. I'm bringing together old photographs and documents to trace
        the histories of festival idols and temple shrines across the city. I'm still digging, and you can
        browse the <a href="/ganeshas-of-mumbai/">Ganeshas of Mumbai archive</a> now.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every Ganesh Chaturthi, my cousin brings home a Ganesh idol. He uses the occasion to raise money,
        usually for an education project. That might mean a lab or toilets for a rural school, or help with school fees and supplies.
        We usually chip in a little.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're in Mumbai during Ganeshotsav, please join us at my family's home for the celebrations.
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Drop me a line</a> if you'd like to come by, hear more, or chip in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="favorite" name="small-favorites">
    <summary>Dosa khakhra</summary>
    <p class="bio">
      One thing I always bring back from Mumbai is dosa khakhra from
      <a href="https://neelamfoodlandmumbai.com/collections/dosa-khakhra">Neelam Foodland</a>,
      a farsan shop in Khar full of snacks and sweets. I get a funny look when I say 'dosa khakhra' to someone
      who's never heard of it. A bite usually clears things up.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="favorite" name="small-favorites">
    <summary>Ratlami snacks</summary>
    <div class="bio">
      <p>
        Part of my family is from Ratlam, and I always bring back a packet of Ratlami sev when I visit.
        It's a crunchy, spicy snack, and I'm pretty particular about where I get mine. Ratlam, every time.
        Most namkeen shops in town will do fine. Ghasiram is a good place to start.
      </p>
      <p>
        I always get potato chips, too. I go to Ghasiram for the straightforward spicy ones and to
        Sanwariya Namkeen for the hing chips when I want that strong hit of asafoetida.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="favorite" name="small-favorites">
    <summary>Permanente Creek Trail</summary>
    <p class="bio">
      Every now and then I take the Permanente Creek Trail in Mountain View. I pick it up in town,
      where it's a paved path, and follow it out to Shoreline, where I can keep walking along the Bay Trail.
      It's flat and relaxing, and on a nice day it's one of my favorite ways to get outside.
      I sometimes "borrow" my roommate's dog for the walk.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="favorite" name="small-favorites">
    <summary>Torrey Pines Gliderport</summary>
    <p class="bio">
      I'd go just to sit on the bluffs and look out over the Pacific. When I was at UC San Diego,
      I kept thinking I'd go gliding here one day. I finally did on a visit back in the summer of 2026,
      and I loved it. If the wind is right when you're there, give it a shot.
      <a href="https://live.flytorrey.com/Home">Check flying conditions</a>.
    </p>
  </details>
</OffClockPage>

<style>
  .favorite {
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .favorite:last-child {
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  summary {
    padding: 0.875rem 0.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .favorite .bio {
    margin-block: 0;
    padding: 0 0.25rem 1.125rem 1.375rem;
  }
</style>
